{"_meta":{"source":"Yahoo Finance via yfinance (profile, statements, analyst estimates)","fetched_at":"2026-11-12T07:42:29+00:00","status":"ok","error":null,"last_success":"2026-11-12T07:42:29+00:00"},"data":{"profile":{"name":"Sanofi","sector":"Healthcare","industry":"Drug Manufacturers - General","country":"France","city":"Paris","website":"https://www.sanofi.com","employees":74846,"summary":"Sanofi engages in the research, development, manufacture, and marketing of therapeutic solutions in Finland and Germany. It provides immunology and inflammation, rare diseases neurology, oncology, and other vaccines. It also offers poliomyelitis, pertussis, and haemophilus influenzae type b (Hib) pediatric vaccines; respiratory syncytial virus protection; hexavalent combination vaccines that includes hepatitis A, typhoid, yellow fever, and rabies vaccines; and Fluzone, a flu vaccine. It has a collaboration and license agreement with Exscientia to develop small-molecule for oncology and immunology; ABL Bio, Inc. to develop ABL301 for treatment of alpha-synucleinopathies; and Innate Pharma SA for cell engager program targeting B7-H3. Further, it has a collaboration agreements with Atomwise to use ATOMNET platform and Insilico Medicine to use Pharma.AI, a medicine's AI platform; Kymera Therapeutics, Inc. to develop and commercialize protein degrader therapies targeting IRAK4 in patients with immune-inflammatory diseases; Nurix Therapeutics, Inc. to develop protein degradation therapies; Denali Therapeutics Inc. to treat systemic inflammatory diseases, such as ulcerative colitis; and Adagene Inc. for development of antibody-based therapies. Additionally, it has a collaboration with Scribe Therapeutics Inc. to develop genome editing technologies; Teva Pharmaceuticals to co-develop and co-commercialize TEV'574, for treatment of ulcerative colitis and Crohn's disease; co-promotion service agreement with Provention Bio, Inc. for the commercialization of teplizumab; and antibody collaboration with Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc. to develop antibodies, such as Dupixent (dupilumab) as treatment for diseases driven by type 2 inflammation. The company was formerly known as Sanofi-Aventis and changed its name to Sanofi in May 2011. Sanofi was incorporated in 1994 and is headquartered in Paris, France.","exchange":"Paris","currency":"EUR","financial_currency":"EUR","summary_fr":"Sanofi se consacre à la recherche, au développement, à la fabrication et à la commercialisation de solutions thérapeutiques en Finlande et en Allemagne. Il fournit l'immunologie et l'inflammation, la neurologie des maladies rares, l'oncologie et d'autres vaccins. Il offre également des vaccins pédiatriques contre la poliomyélite, la coqueluche et l'haemophilus influenzae de type b (Hib); protection contre le virus respiratoire syncytial; vaccins combinés hexavalents comprenant les vaccins contre l'hépatite A, la typhoïde, la fièvre jaune et la rage; et Fluzone, un vaccin contre la grippe."},"valuation":{"market_cap_yahoo":103764738048,"shares_outstanding":1198068685,"trailing_pe":25.250729,"forward_pe":9.188464,"price_to_book":1.4260781,"ev_to_ebitda":7.999,"ev_to_revenue":2.318,"dividend_yield":0.0479,"payout_ratio":1.1908001,"beta_yahoo":0.256},"targets":{"current_price":86.61,"mean":95.70435,"median":99.0,"high":110.0,"low":78.0,"n_analysts":23,"reco_mean":2.125,"reco_key":"buy"},"calendar":{"earnings_dates":["2027-01-28"],"eps_avg":1.7246,"eps_low":1.37128,"eps_high":2.11,"revenue_avg":12910876500,"ex_dividend":"2026-05-05","dividend_date":null},"holders":{"insiders_pct":0.10313,"institutions_pct":0.41984,"institutions_float_pct":0.46811,"institutions_n":856,"institutions":[{"name":"Pacer Advisors, Inc.","pct":0.001,"shares":1156434,"value":100158749,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.2836},{"name":"Gamma Investing LLC","pct":0.0,"shares":17,"value":1472,"date":"2026-09-30","chg":-0.7069},{"name":"Generali Investments Cee, Investicni Spolecnost, A.s.","pct":0.0,"shares":29339,"va